aarch64: do not export _SecCertificateCopyPublicKey_ios on arm64.

On arm64 macOS SecCertificate.c aliases the _ios implementation to the plain
_SecCertificateCopyPublicKey symbol (TARGET_CPU_ARM64 branch), so the _ios symbol
name does not exist and the exported-symbols list fails to resolve it when linking
Security. Guard the export with !TARGET_CPU_ARM64; the base name is already exported.
Matches darling-security upstream (this pin is byte-identical to that PR base).
--- a/OSX/sec/Security/SecExports.exp-in
+++ b/OSX/sec/Security/SecExports.exp-in
@@ -504,7 +504,9 @@
 _SecCertificateCopyNormalizedSubjectContent
 _SecCertificateCopyPreference
 _SecCertificateCopyPreferred
+#if !TARGET_CPU_ARM64
 _SecCertificateCopyPublicKey_ios
+#endif
 _SecCertificateCopyPublicKeySHA1DigestFromCertificateData
 _SecCertificateCopyShortDescription
 _SecCertificateCopySubjectComponent
